hor="end" transform="translate(67.91999816894531 235.33333333333331)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">30</text><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="79.91999816894531" y1="251.55555555555554" x2="365" y2="251.55555555555554" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"/><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="73.91999816894531" y1="251.55555555555554" x2="85.91999816894531" y2="251.55555555555554" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"/><text text-anchor="end" transform="translate(67.91999816894531 257.55555555555554)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">20</text><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="79.91999816894531" y1="273.77777777777777" x2="365" y2="273.77777777777777" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"/><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="73.91999816894531" y1="273.77777777777777" x2="85.91999816894531" y2="273.77777777777777" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"/><text text-anchor="end" transform="translate(67.91999816894531 279.77777777777777)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">10</text><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="79.91999816894531" y1="296" x2="365" y2="296" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"/><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="73.91999816894531" y1="296" x2="85.91999816894531" y2="296" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"/><text text-anchor="end" transform="translate(67.91999816894531 302)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">0</text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(24 196) rotate(-90)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Percent of drawings</text><line xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x1="79.91999816894531" y1="96" x2="79.91999816894531" y2="296" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.9"/><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="120.64571271623885" y="117.11111111111111" height="178.88888888888889" width="40.72571454729353" fill="#B3B3B3" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><text xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="end" transform="translate(150.9285699898856 315.84) rotate(-40)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">mammals</text><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="202.09714181082592" y="143.55555555555557" height="152.44444444444443" width="40.72571454729353" fill="#B3B3B3" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><text xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="end" transform="translate(232.37999908447267 315.84) rotate(-40)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">birds</text><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="283.548570905413" y="174.66666666666666" height="121.33333333333334" width="40.72571454729353" fill="#B3B3B3" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><text xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="end" transform="translate(313.8314281790598 315.84) rotate(-40)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">insects</text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(222.45999908447266 24)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Percent of Drawings</text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(222.45999908447266 48)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Containing an Example of</text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(222.45999908447266 72)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Each Animal Group</text><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" x="171.9609603881836" y="414.2607421875" height="26.84" width="100.99807739257812" stroke="#000000" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="178.9609603881836" y="421.2607421875" height="12" width="12" fill="#B3B3B3" stroke="#000000" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><text transform="translate(197.9609603881836 433.2607421875)" text-anchor="top" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Animal</text></g></svg></figure><div class="sr-only" role="region" aria-label="Long description for bar graph titled Percent of Drawings Containing an Example of Each Animal Group"><ul>
<li>The Percent of drawings data for the 3 bars are as follows:<br/>
<ul>
<li>mammals: 80.5&nbsp;</li>
<li>birds: 68.6</li>
<li>insects: 54.6</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div>
<p>Researchers Kate Howlett and Edgar Turner asked 401 schoolchildren in the United Kingdom to draw and label local wildlife. The researchers suggest that the children may be more aware of mammals than of other animals in their environments.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes data from the graph that support the researchers&rsquo; conclusion?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"49cb926d-9b0e-49f6-b62d-524fbb75dd4d","content":"<p>There were about as many drawings with an example of an insect as there were with an example of a bird.</p>"},{"id":"bda201c8-1f81-434e-9226-24fa77f99878","content":"<p>The fewest number of drawings contained an example of a bird.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"9c415071-f7fe-4814-8858-2952bfef81ac","content":"<p>More of the drawings had an example of an insect than an example of a mammal.</p>"},{"id":"609f5fec-a230-4425-af4f-6aafc7551810","content":"<p>More of the drawings had an example of a mammal than either an example of a bird or an example of an insect.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["609f5fec-a230-4425-af4f-6aafc7551810"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it accurately describes data from the graph that support the researchers&rsquo; conclusion that children may be more aware of mammals than of other animals. The graph presents the percent of drawings by schoolchildren that contained an example of an animal from a certain group (mammals, birds, or insects). The graph shows that approximately 80% of the drawings contained an example of a mammal, while only approximately 69% contained an example of a bird and only about 55% contained an example of an insect. The fact that mammals were included in more drawings than either birds or insects were supports the idea that children may be particularly aware of mammals in their environments.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the graph shows that there were not "about as many" drawings with insects as there were drawings with birds (approximately 69% of the drawings included an example of a bird, while only about 55% included an example of an insect). Further, comparing only the numbers for birds and insects wouldn&rsquo;t indicate anything about the schoolchildren&rsquo;s awareness of mammals. Choice B is incorrect because the graph shows that insects, not birds, were the group that appeared in the fewest number of drawings (approximately 69% of the drawings included an example of a bird but only about 55% included an example of an insect). Further, stating that examples from one nonmammal group appeared in the fewest number of drawings would provide no evidence about the schoolchildren&rsquo;s awareness of mammals. Choice C is incorrect because the graph shows that more drawings had an example of a mammal than an example of an insect, not the other way around (approximately 80% of the drawings included an example of a mammal, while only about 55% included an example of an insect). Further, examples of a nonmammal group appearing in more drawings than examples of mammals did would actually weaken the claim that schoolchildren may be more aware of mammals than of other animals.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"0b634641","external_id":"7920d9f7-7b71-430c-bc7c-ebcf5d8c1779","vaultid":null,"uId":"a168b545-3617-4119-9541-5d12a3038bb3","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"INI","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill_cd":"COE","skill_desc":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<figure class=\"image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"380\" height=\"452.1007080078125\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 452.1007080078125\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar graph titled Percent of Drawings Containing an Example of Each Animal Group. The horizontal axis is labeled Animal. 3 bars are shown. The vertical axis is labeled Percent of drawings. It ranges from 0 to 90 in increments